      "side": 1,
      "message": "Benson, Nathan: This CL is based on the \"Functionally connect the USB TX/RX pairs\" language from the \"Attached.SRC Requirements\" and \"Attached.SNK Requirements\" sections of the Type-C spec.\n\nUp to this point, we\u0027ve been doing this at slightly different times and I think typically waiting to set USB mode until we\u0027ve seen USB data communication in PD responses (implying that PD is supported). It would take me a bit to fully describe when we currently set the mux mode to USB.\n\nDo you know if our current practice is based on anything in particular? Is this just a requirement that we\u0027ve missed accidentally up to this point?",
      "revId": "fee06cf333fa2c34fb8fd7f0cebd46e866161fed",
